Derive the following Finite Equally Spaced N-Level Systems relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
C_{V,1}=k_{\mathrm B}x^2\left[
\frac{e^x}{(e^x-1)^2}
-\frac{M^2e^{Mx}}{(e^{Mx}-1)^2}
\right].
\tag*{[4]}
\]
Notation: \(M,j\) denotes number of levels and level index, from 0 to M-1; unit \(\mathrm{1, 1}\); \(\epsilon_j\) denotes energy of level j; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\hbar,\omega\) denotes reduced Planck constant and angular frequency setting the level spacing; unit \(\mathrm{J s, rad s^{-1}}\); \(T,k_{\mathrm B},\beta,x\) denotes temperature, Boltzmann constant, inverse thermal energy, and beta hbar omega; unit \(\mathrm{K, J K^{-1}, J^{-1}, 1}\); \(q,z_1\) denotes Boltzmann ratio exp(-x) and one-particle partition function; unit \(\mathrm{1, 1}\); \(u,s,C_{V,1}\) denotes one-particle mean energy, entropy, and constant-volume heat capacity; unit \(\mathrm{J, J K^{-1}, J K^{-1}}\).
